cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt Strata 0–3, please cite this repository and identify the exact release."
title: "Strata 0–3: A Reasoning and Alignment Scaffold for AI Systems"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Frank
    family-names: Böhm
version: "0.5-draft"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proposed reasoning scaffold intended to support epistemic honesty, boundary
  discipline, corrigibility, useful refusal, and escalation in artificial-intelligence
  systems. Development included private adversarial review and limited historical
  synthetic next-action tests, not evidence of causal benefit or deployment safety.
  See the README for the tested-version boundary and evidence limitations.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - alignment
  - system prompts
  - corrigibility
  - epistemic uncertainty
  - refusal
  - adversarial review
